+### Refunds 
 
-  No
+You can issue a full or partial refund for an FPX payment within 180 days of the original payment through the [Dashboard](https://dashboard.stripe.com/payments) or [Refunds API](https://docs.stripe.com/api/refunds/create.md). FPX refunds are asynchronous and normally take up to 14 days to complete, but can take up to 6 weeks. You can’t cancel an FPX refund after submitting it.
 
-- **Refunds / Partial refunds**
+#### Refund process 
 
-  [Yes / Yes](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/fpx.md#refunds)
+FPX refunds are always processed as a separate credit to the customer’s bank account. Unlike card payments, they’re never issued as a reversal. The refund won’t be explicitly labeled as a refund on the customer’s bank statement. Instead, it appears as a credit referencing the original payment’s statement descriptor. We recommend notifying your customer when you issue a refund so they can identify the incoming credit.
 
-- **Dispute support**
+#### Tracking refunds 
 
-  [No](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/fpx.md#disputed-payments)
+To check a refund’s status, open the payment in the [Dashboard](https://dashboard.stripe.com/payments) and click **View details** on the refund entry. You can also [retrieve the Refund object](https://docs.stripe.com/api/refunds/retrieve.md) and check its `status` field.
 
-- **Manual capture support**
+Stripe notifies you of the final status through a `refund.updated` or `refund.failed` *webhook* (A webhook is a real-time push notification sent to your application as a JSON payload through HTTPS requests) event. [Verify webhook signatures](https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks.md#verify-events) to confirm that events came from Stripe. You can also use Stripe’s [public IP addresses](https://docs.stripe.com/ips.md) for network allowlisting. When a refund succeeds, the [Refund object](https://docs.stripe.com/api/refunds/object.md) status changes to `succeeded`. If the refund fails, the status changes to `failed` and Stripe returns the amount to your Stripe balance. You must refund the customer using another method.
 
-  No
+### Disputes 
 
-- **Connect support**
+FPX requires customers to authenticate payments directly with their bank, which reduces the risk of fraud and unrecognized transactions. As a result, FPX doesn’t support the standard dispute process—customers can’t file a chargeback through their bank, and funds are never withdrawn from your Stripe balance because of a dispute.
 
-  Yes
+If a customer contacts their bank about a payment made with FPX, the bank directs them back to you. You can then issue a full or partial refund.
 
