-## Refunds
-
-FPX payments can be refunded up to 60 days after the original payment. Refunds for FPX payments are asynchronous and take approximately 1 week to complete. We’ll notify you of the final refund status using the `refund.updated` or `refund.failed` *webhook* (A webhook is a real-time push notification sent to your application as a JSON payload through HTTPS requests) event. When a refund succeeds, the [Refund](https://docs.stripe.com/api/refunds/object.md) object’s status transitions to `succeeded`. A refund can fail if the customer’s bank is unable to process it correctly (for example, the bank account is closed). In the rare instance that a refund fails, the Refund object’s status transitions to `failed` and we return the amount to your Stripe balance. You then need to arrange an alternative way of providing your customer with a refund.+If your integration lists payment methods manually, learn how to [configure FPX as a payment method](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/fpx/accept-a-payment.md).